.* FILE2: the task menu for more file tasks.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 2'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPTION CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=PANELID CLASS=NAMECL VALUE='FILE2'.
:IMPORT NAME=WRKDDMF PNLGRP=QHDDCMD.
:KEYL NAME=MENUKEYS HELP='KEYS/MENUKEYS'.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F13 ACTION='MENU INFO'.F13=Information Assistant
:KEYI KEY=F16 ACTION='MENU MAIN'.F16=System Main menu
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=FILE2 HELP=HLPFILE2 KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM PANELID=PANELID.Files
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES OPTIONS=OPTION.Select one of the following:
:MENUI OPTION=1 ACTION='CMD ?WRKDDMF' HELP=WRKDDMF.Work with Distributed Data Management (DDM) Files
:MENUI OPTION=2 ACTION='MENU FILETFR' HELP='FILE2/OPT2'.Send or receive files
:MENUI OPTION=3 ACTION='MENU CMDCRTF' HELP='FILE2/OPT3'.Create a file
:MENUI OPTION=4 ACTION='CMD EDTRBDAP' HELP='FILE2/OPT4'.Edit rebuild of access paths
:MENUI OPTION=50 ACTION='CMD ?SAVS36F' HELP='FILE2/OPT50'.Save a file in System/36 format
:MENUI OPTION=51 ACTION='CMD ?RSTS36F' HELP='FILE2/OPT51'.Restore a file from System/36 format
:MENUI OPTION=70 ACTION='MENU CMDFIL' HELP='FILE2/OPT70'.Related commands
:EMENU.
:CMDLINE SIZE=LONG.Selection or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPFILE2.Files - Help
:P.The second page of file tasks: remote files, transfers, creating files
and the access paths waiting to be rebuilt.
:P.Type an option number or a command and press Enter. F4 prompts the
command, F9 brings the previous one back, F12 returns to the menu shown
before this one.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/MENUKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F13=Information Assistant
:PD.Shows menu INFO.
:PT.F16=System Main menu
:PD.Shows menu MAIN.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FILE2/OPT2'.Send or receive files
:P.Option 2. Shows menu FILETFR&colon. Send or receive files.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FILE2/OPT3'.Create a file
:P.Option 3. Shows menu CMDCRTF&colon. Create a file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FILE2/OPT4'.Edit rebuild of access paths
:P.Option 4. Runs the EDTRBDAP command&colon. Edit rebuild of access
paths.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FILE2/OPT50'.Save a file in System/36 format
:P.Option 50. Runs the SAVS36F command&colon. Save a file in System/36
format.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FILE2/OPT51'.Restore a file from System/36 format
:P.Option 51. Runs the RSTS36F command&colon. Restore a file from
System/36 format.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FILE2/OPT70'.Related commands
:P.Option 70. Shows menu CMDFIL&colon. Related commands.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
